**Step 1. Helper** fresh under `.tools/b2115/` (one file with sub-commands, `b2115.py`; give every quarantine name a unique suffix) with a `selftest` that shows, against scratch copies and a FAKE Jira and GitHub transport only (no request leaves the process in the selftest): each scanner rule firing (the six planted cases of THE TEXT RULES); a frozen text one character off; the C-89 proof refusing a planted change of one old byte and a C-number with a gap; the BACKLOG proof refusing a planted change of one byte on an old line, a planted tick (`[ ]` to `[x]`) of item 85 or of item 106, a tick of item 94 that changes a second byte of its line, a missing tick of item 146, BL-CLOSE-93 inserted one line off (before item 93's `    - Discovered:` line, and after item 94's first line), BL-PART-85 inserted after item 86's first line, BL-CLOSE-143 and BL-CLOSE-146 swapped, the four new items inserted after item 146's block instead of 147's, an empty line between two new items, and a proof that removes added lines by text instead of by position (control: a planted copy of one new line elsewhere); P-4 refusing a scratch `BACKLOG.md` whose highest owed number is 148, one where item 133 is already `[x]`, and one where item 147's block has a line after its `Discovered:` line; P-5 refusing a planted line-3 entry not ending `(records seat)`; P-L refusing a `main` sha that is not c73cda4c, a pull request numbered 55, a file list of pull request 54 with one path changed (compared as a whole list), a squash with two parents, a squash whose tree is not dd15534f, and a landed first line that differs from the review's subject with `#54`; HOLD R refusing a target that changed under the build; HOLD R2 rebuilding once on a target changed between read and replace; THE JIRA FENCE refusing each of its cases (a PUT, a DELETE, a POST to `/rest/api/3/issue`, a POST to `/rest/api/3/issue/OXPD2-1/transitions`, a comment to OXPD2-62, a 2nd POST, a planted `.env` value in a text, the slot not WRITE); THE SKIP RULE skipping a planted equal comment and stopping on a planted near-duplicate (and NOT stopping on a planted comment starting `Records pass after pull request 53`); a read-back with one block changed reading UNEQUAL; the GitHub GET-only fence refusing a `gh` verb that is not `api -X GET`. Selftest output to scratch paths only. **Build each record file only from its OWN live bytes at its own write.** A `panes` sub-command decodes the pane list (never print raw start commands; an unnamed pane is a line with an empty name: do not strip it away, B2105's D4).
**Step 2. Facts and PRIOR WORK.** Write `SOURCES READ WHOLE` by PROGRAM (a sub-command, never the Write tool) into `.tools/b2115/facts/sources-read.txt` before the first write, listing what you read whole and what by range. Re-hash every row of THE SOURCES (a difference is named, and judged as THE SOURCES says). P-1 to P-8; P-L; P-F (fetch and extract the tarball, run your own program over it, print the pointers with their fragments and the controls); P-J.
**Step 3. Texts by program (dry run):** check every frozen sha256; fill everything (`<<C-89>>` from P-7; `<<BL-OLD8>>` from your before-copy, `<<BL-NEW8>>` from the dry `BACKLOG.md`; `<<CMT-1>>` as `00000`); run both scanners; write the would-be record files into `dry/` and print for each its line feeds before and after and the added, removed and changed line counts (PREDICTED in THE DRY-RUN FIGURES); build the comment body and print its blocks and codes. Print every filled line whole once and read it. Slot RECORDS HOLD stops here with `RECORDS DRY RUN ONLY`.
**Step 4. Writes** (slot RECORDS WRITE; HOLD stops at Step 3): re-read the panes (REFUSE 5); re-run P-2, P-3, P-4, P-5, P-7, P-L and P-J on the live bytes and origin; then, in this order: **4a** `CLARIFICATIONS.md`; **4b** `BACKLOG.md` (each by HOLD R and its PART's proof); **4c** Jira (slot JIRA WRITE; with JIRA HOLD stop after 4b with the last line `STOPPED: NEEDS TUESDAY jira held after 4b`, since H-JIRA names the comment id); **4d** `history.md` by HOLD R and HOLD R2, its `<<BL-NEW8>>` from 4b's print. Prove each: the proofs of its PART, 0 bytes above 126 in the added bytes, no `<<` left, no temp file left, sha256 before and after; P-6's files unchanged. Print the new and changed lines back BY THEIR NEW POSITIONS. **A failure after the first write:** stop at once; what is written stays as written (never undone by you); STATUS names which writes are done and which are not, and the last line is `STOPPED: NEEDS TUESDAY <file or J-1> not written after <check>`.
**Step 5. STATUS** sections: Questions, BLUF, Step 0, SOURCES READ WHOLE, PRIOR WORK, Facts re-measured (with controls), Records (the proofs), Jira (the write log), HELD, NOT RUN, FOR TUESDAY, Deviations (which files were read in parts), Corrections.

## CLOCK AND HARD STOP
RECORDS DONE by your Step-0 clock plus 45 minutes, HARD STOP plus 75 (the Stamp's Hard stop slot gives the absolute outer limit; whichever is earlier). No record or Jira write from HARD STOP minus 10. At the hard stop with work left: the HANDOVER form. The drafter sized this pass at about 30 to 45 minutes of one seat (B2105's seat wrote three files, two ticks and one POST and read GitHub and a tarball; this pass adds five more ticks, one part line and one more new item, and no re-scan reads).

